From: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: de10nano: grow the MiSTer_fb region to 24 MiB

Origin:       original, this repo (not from the fork, not upstream).
Author:       Michael C. Ferguson; applies on top of 0004 (and, in the beta
              series, after 0043/0046, whose nodes it does not touch).
Upstream:     No (MiSTer-specific node).
Disposition:  carry -- approved by the owner 2026-11-13. Depends on 0070.

reg grows from <0x22000000 0x800000> (8 MiB) to <0x22000000 0x1800000>
(24 MiB, ending 0x237fffff), so with 0070's smem_len a /dev/fb0 mmap
reaches two 1080p 8888 frames (2 x 8,294,400 B = 15.8 MiB, plus the 4 KiB
header page), not just two 565 frames.

Why this extent:
- it matches legacy Main's own over-map, shmem_map(FB_ADDR, FB_SIZE*4*3)
  = 0x22000000-0x237bafff (Main_MiSTer video.cpp:2414): legacy already
  treats those bytes as its framebuffers (buffer 0 = fb0, buffers 1-2 =
  menu backgrounds) on every core;
- it stays below 0x24000000, where the Menu core's DDR wipe and SMS's
  screen-rotation framebuffer start.

Why it needs 0070: stock's `mode` write memsets the whole resource. Over
24 MiB that would wipe legacy's menu-background buffers on every mode
write; 0070 clears only the header page and the visible frame.

SNES MSU-1: the core's MSU data store skips an absolute 8 MiB hole at
0x22000000-0x227FFFFF, and the track base is whatever Main sends at run
time. Stock Main sends a base that puts the track's post-hole part at
0x22800000+ while a .msu is mounted, i.e. inside this grown window -- but
stock Main's own video_menu_bg buffers already over-map those bytes
(video.cpp:2414), so the overlap is stock's own, not new here, and stock
Main never mmaps /dev/fb0. The greenfield rewrite sends base 0x23000000
and writes the track linearly from 0x23800000, so the whole window
0x22000000-0x237FFFFF is free for the framebuffer on every core it runs;
no per-core 8 MiB carve-out is needed.

The memremap() grows from 8 to 24 MiB of vmalloc space; with mem=511M
the ARM vmalloc area is several hundred MiB, so this is well within it.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/intel/socfpga/socfpga_cyclone5_de10nano.dts | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/intel/socfpga/socfpga_cyclone5_de10nano.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/intel/socfpga/socfpga_cyclone5_de10nano.dts
@@ -125,7 +125,12 @@
 	 */
 	MiSTer_fb@22000000 {
 		compatible = "MiSTer_fb";
-		reg = <0x22000000 0x800000>;
+		/*
+		 * 24 MiB, 0x22000000-0x237fffff: legacy Main's own over-map
+		 * extent, below the Menu core's wipe at 0x24000000.  Needs
+		 * patch 0070 (the mode write clears only the visible frame).
+		 */
+		reg = <0x22000000 0x1800000>;
 		interrupt-parent = <&intc>;
 		interrupts = <0 40 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 	};
